.TH tensor-wasm-invoke 1  "tensor-wasm-invoke "
.SH NAME
tensor\-wasm\-invoke \- Invoke a previously deployed function by id
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtensor\-wasm invoke\fR \fB\-\-server\fR=\fISERVER\fR [\fB\-\-args\fR=\fIARGS\fR] [\fB\-\-tenant\fR=\fITENANT\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIID\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
POSTs \fB{server}/functions/{id}/invoke\fR with a JSON body. When \fB\-\-args\fR is supplied it is parsed and validated to be a JSON array, then forwarded as the request body; otherwise an empty object is sent. The successful response body is pretty\-printed to stdout. A non\-2xx response is rendered through the shared error\-envelope helper and the process exits non\-zero.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR=\fISERVER\fR
Base URL of the target TensorWasm server (e.g. \fBhttp://localhost:8080\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-args\fR=\fIARGS\fR
Arguments forwarded to the function, encoded as a JSON array.
.TP
\fB\-\-tenant\fR=\fITENANT\fR [default: 0]
Tenant id to advertise on outbound API requests.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIID\fR]
Identifier of the deployed function to invoke.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBTENSOR_WASM_TOKEN\fR
Bearer token attached as \fBAuthorization: Bearer ...\fR on the outbound request when set.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
tensor\-wasm(1), tensor\-wasm\-deploy(1)
